                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_434">Oxford, Oxfordshire. St Mary
                        Magdalen College</orgName><p>Four manuscripts now bound together. Notes in
                        the hand of John Dygon appear on one (fols. 124–139), but it is not clear
                        that they were bound together in the Middle Ages. Part at least certainly
                        came to the College in the later sixteenth century.‘Liber Collegij beatae
                        mariae magdalene ex dono Mr Bolderne’ (fol. 1, s. xvi/xvii, referring to
                        John Bolderne (d. 1577), fellow of Magdalen)Perhaps John Dygon (d. after
